{"entry": "14657", "subentry": "14657002", "pointer": "", "decision": "fix-unit", "rule": "D6_HAND_SLIP", "reason": "CAPSET-v2 D6: Y-89(n,g)Y-90m thermal Maxwellian (SIG,,MXW), Krane 2020, EXFOR 14657002: DATA 1.02 / 0.98 / 1.06 B with ERR-T 0.01-0.03 B for three irradiation positions. The other EXFOR measurements of the same isomeric thermal cross section are 1 mb: Heath 1961 11870002 (0.001 B, MXW), De Corte 1988 23488032 (0.00104 B), Farina Arbocco 2013 23266090/91 (0.00107 B). The compiled unit B is a x1000 slip for MB. fix-unit, factor 0.001 (trust 0 until the correction is applied at ingest).", "reviewer": "agent:claude-opus-5.5", "date": "2026-11-06", "factor": 0.001}
{"entry": "13947", "subentry": "13947004", "pointer": "", "decision": "fix-unit", "rule": "D6_HAND_SLIP", "reason": "CAPSET-v2 D6: Ni-60(n,g)Ni-61 partial gamma-ray cross sections (PAR,SIG,,MXW), Raman et al. 2004, EXFOR 13947004 (Table 10): 240 gamma lines compiled in B that sum to 3693 B (e.g. 812 B at E-gamma 283 keV), while the same quantity from Gippner 1971 (30150003, 31 lines compiled in MB) sums to 2744 MB; a thermal capture cross section of a few barns times a gamma multiplicity of a few cannot give thousands of barns of gamma lines. The values are millibarns. fix-unit, factor 0.001.", "reviewer": "agent:claude-opus-5.5", "date": "2026-11-06", "factor": 0.001}
{"entry": "41639", "subentry": "41639002", "pointer": "", "decision": "exclude", "rule": "D6_HAND_SLIP", "reason": "CAPSET-v2 D6: Sb-124(n,g)Sb-125 spectrum average (SIG,,SPA), Murin 1957 (At. Energy 2, 552), EXFOR 41639002: one DATA-APRX value 2000 B with no uncertainty, at an incident energy the compiler supposed (COMMENT: 'Incident neutron energy is not given in the article, supposed by compiler as 0.0253 eV'; HISTORY 2021 changed EN-DUMMY from 1 MeV). Excluded on the record: an approximate value of a quantity whose energy is not defined. It is NOT proven to be a unit slip: Courtemanche 1966 (11990002, SPA) gives 6.5 B, x300 lower, but Elgart 1971 (10728004, MXW) gives 2990 B, the same magnitude as this value, so EXFOR alone does not settle Sb-124; 10728004 and 11990002 are left to the automatic layer and listed for a person to read.", "reviewer": "agent:claude-opus-5.5", "date": "2026-11-06"}
